# Trivy ignore list — the triaged-exception file for the image
# vulnerability gates (issue #481: the ci.yml `audit` job scan of the
# locally-built image + the release.yml post-push scans of the published
# image, both running with `--severity CRITICAL,HIGH --exit-code 1`).
#
# Usage: one vulnerability identifier (CVE-… or GHSA-…) per line; `#`
# starts a comment and blank lines are skipped. An id listed here is
# excluded from the CRITICAL/HIGH failure in BOTH gates (they share this
# file on purpose — an exception must not be narrower than the triage).
#
# Triage rules:
#   * Only list ids that have been INVESTIGATED, not merely observed:
#     each entry needs an adjacent justification comment (why it is not
#     exploitable in this image — e.g. the vulnerable code path is never
#     executed by the operator) and a follow-up issue owning the rebuild.
#   * Never delete a gate to make a finding pass; add the id here.
#   * Re-review entries on every base-image digest bump (#124) and
#     lockfile bump — an entry whose fixing version has shipped should
#     be deleted in the same PR.
#
# There are currently no triaged exceptions — keep it that way unless a
# real triage happens.
